WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.050
Every photon in a laser
beam is paid for in advance.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.770
All the energy in the
beam comes from the pump:

3
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.850
a flash lamp, say, or an electric current.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.190
The pump lifts atoms to
higher energy levels.

5
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.800
But give the atoms only two levels,
and no laser will ever work.

6
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.250
Why can't two levels ever be enough?

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.770
And why do four do better than three?

8
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.850
In this mission, you'll climb the energy
ladders of three-level and four-level

9
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.270
lasers, rung by rung.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.710
Then you'll meet the semiconductor laser:

11
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.370
tiny, cheap, and far more
efficient than other types.

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.290
Your mission: explain why a
laser can't work with two levels,

13
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.170
and why four beat three.
